1
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:24,860
Catching the winds of the passing seasons,
shining in the greatest harmony

2
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:37,460
Leaping lightly past these hectic times,
diving into the town with a flashy air

3
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,460
I wanna dive into paradise

4
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:49,140
Rather than chasing the latest fashions,
it's your bare face that sets the pace

5
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,040
Let it break!

6
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do it,
the dreams we set running never stop

7
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,400
Let's set sail for tomorrow too! Let it run!

8
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,660
Everybody can do it, just a little

9
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,800
Stepping outside the lines won't hurt a bit

10
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,000
Holding onto a restless curiosity

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,060
Strong and high, fly high

12
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,460
The Ohara family treasure

13
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,900
Hey, are you sure this road is really okay?

14
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:48,620
Yeah, I think it's probably a recently built road,
don't you think?

15
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,620
Considering it doesn't even
show up on the car navigation,

16
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,460
we haven't passed a single
oncoming car since earlier.

17
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,260
What about you, Honda?

18
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,920
If we're still on the main road,
there's no mistake.

19
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,460
It's been one straight road the whole time.

20
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:05,080
But Chief, do you really commute
all the way from a place like this?

21
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:09,900
Yes. From the JR, then a facility,
then a bus, and then a 20-minute walk.

22
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:12,180
All told,
it apparently takes two and a half hours.

23
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:15,680
Five hours round trip?
That's enough to make me faint.

24
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:19,860
By the way, Ryo-chan, what did you end up
buying for the Chief's birthday present?

25
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,860
It's a secret until we arrive.

26
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:27,500
Come on, we all pooled our money together,
so you could at least tell us.

27
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:32,460
Don't worry. I picked out a
special item myself. No mistake.

28
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:34,360
That's not what I mean.

29
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:39,640
I'm saying it's strange that the people giving
the present don't even know what they're giving.

30
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:40,540
Exactly.

31
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:45,640
Let's just say it's the most
wonderful thing there is.

32
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:50,080
Chief, when he sees this, he's sure
to be so moved he'll fall right over.

33
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:55,080
We've somehow entered a residential area.

34
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,100
We should be getting close by now.

35
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:00,900
Still, this scenery is kind of lonely,
isn't it.

36
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:11,860
Wait, wait, wait,
what are you doing all of a sudden, senpai?

37
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:15,040
S-senpai...

38
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,980
Excuse me, may I ask you something?

39
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,640
Do you happen to know
where Ohara's house is?

40
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:30,060
Then it's about another kilometer ahead.

41
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:31,058
I see,

42
00:03:31,108 --> 00:03:34,780
if it's all right,
please get in the car and guide us.

43
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,640
We'll take you there properly.

44
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:40,640
But it's a single road,
so there's no way you'll get lost.

45
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:44,380
Come on, don't say that. Don't they
say a journey is better with company?

46
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:47,480
The moment he sees a pretty woman,
it's always this with you.

47
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,840
Get out, Honda, this man's riding with us.

48
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,980
So what am I supposed to do?

49
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:57,760
Hey, they say it's close even if we walk.

50
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:00,720
In that case, we don't need him to guide us.

51
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:03,820
You don't have to force me to ride along.

52
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:06,640
Excuse me, please wait a moment.

53
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,600
He's telling me to get out right away.

54
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,140
Senpai, this car can fit five people.

55
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,940
Shut up, Nakagawa! I hate being cramped!

56
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:16,540
Ryo-chan, poor Mr. Honda.

57
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,260
Hurry up and sit down!

58
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:19,120
Honda!

59
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:22,060
Don't you feel bad keeping Hedy waiting?

60
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,960
N-no way...

61
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:26,360
Shino, you're not riding,
so hurry up and get out!

62
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,660
Hurry up, go ahead, go ahead!

63
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:33,680
I wonder why it always
turns out like this...

64
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:36,200
Honestly,
why does it always end up like this!

65
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:40,000
So you're going to celebrate
your boss's birthday?

66
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:44,180
Yes, it's one of those
social obligations of life.

67
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:48,900
That must be tough, coming all the way out
into the mountains on your precious day off.

68
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:54,460
Honestly, who would build a house in
a place where tanuki might show up?

69
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:58,640
Excuse me, miss,
do you live around here too?

70
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:05,100
Well, even so, to have a birthday
celebration thrown for you...

71
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,940
That person must be really well
liked by their subordinates.

72
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:12,500
Not at all, they're extremely diligent and honest,
and they never even listen to the news.

73
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:17,440
Being that well liked isn't something
just anyone can manage, is it.

74
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,180
Whoa.

75
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:23,540
It must be unfortunate to have
to work under someone like that.

76
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:26,220
You've got to keep them in
a good mood now and then.

77
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:29,760
In your case, senpai,
you cause a lot of trouble.

78
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,540
It's me who's being troubled here!

79
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:34,260
It's over there.

80
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,780
So this is the Chief's house.

81
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,736
A tiny veranda,

82
00:05:45,786 --> 00:05:48,800
a garden squeezed in with great effort,
and even a garden pavilion.

83
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:52,834
But really,
just to build this tiny little house,

84
00:05:52,884 --> 00:05:55,340
all that sweat and tears
must have gone into it.

85
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:00,260
Right, we have to take you
all the way to your home.

86
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,640
No, that's fine. I'm here too.

87
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,420
Because this is my home, you see.

88
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:10,482
So that means,

89
00:06:10,532 --> 00:06:12,360
could it be...?

90
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:19,920
...smelly-footed and inflexible, I'm Hiromi, the boss's daughter.
Welcome, everyone!

91
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:27,160
Well, that's the Chief's... yes. So you've
been aware of it since earlier, right?

92
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:35,820
I've heard all about Ryo-san and the others from my father.
I've always deeply respected the Chief.

93
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:36,573
Eh,

94
00:06:36,623 --> 00:06:40,440
The Chief truly is a model
for all police officers, yes!

95
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,450
You don't have to force yourself, you know.
Because,

96
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:46,180
my father really is just like that.

97
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,100
Eh, right?

98
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,500
Whoa-ho!

99
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:57,740
We've arrived too.

100
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:03,140
I'm home. Hey, Dad. We have guests.

101
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,700
Who could it be, all of a sudden?

102
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,640
Hello, hello!

103
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:10,520
What are you lot doing here?

104
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,380
Don't say it like that. Come on.

105
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,120
Your adoring subordinates
came to see their boss

106
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,060
all the way from afar, didn't we?

107
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,920
Love turns to hate a hundredfold!

108
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:21,240
Welcome, everyone.

109
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:22,480
Sorry.

110
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,020
For barging in on you all at once like this.

111
00:07:25,020 --> 00:07:26,060
Hello.

112
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,920
Come on in.

113
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:29,840
Excuse us.

114
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:32,380
Right this way, right this way.

115
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,923
What a fine home you have. The construction of this entranceway,
for one,

116
00:07:35,973 --> 00:07:38,239
is so compact and well put together,

117
00:07:38,289 --> 00:07:41,580
it really shows the
Chief's modest character.

118
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:45,306
And this wallpaper has
such a down-to-earth charm,

119
00:07:45,356 --> 00:07:49,746
designed so that visitors
don't feel any tension.

120
00:07:49,796 --> 00:07:51,540
You don't need to come in!

121
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:56,092
What are you saying, Dad?
They came all this way.

122
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,920
Come on in, Ryotsu-san.

123
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:02,680
Who knew the Chief had such a cute daughter?

124
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:05,560
Should we say a kite
has given birth to a swan?

125
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,900
Hey, Ryotsu.

126
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:08,420
I'm telling you this once, so listen.

127
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:10,060
Don't get any funny ideas.

128
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:13,460
Hiromi, a rough guy like you,

129
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:15,240
I can't imagine her having
any feelings for you.

130
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:17,940
Yeah, yeah, I'm a rough guy, what of it?

131
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:19,760
Not as rough as you, Chief.

132
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,960
W-what did you say?

133
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,540
Dad, stop it!

134
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:24,340
This isn't the workplace, you know.

135
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:26,840
Sorry, sorry.

136
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:34,140
Well... still, what's gotten into you,
suddenly coming at me like this?

137
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,720
Really? You have no idea at all?

138
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:47,380
Happy birthday, Dad!
Happy birthday, Chief! Congratulations!

139
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:54,380
Congratulations! Congratulations!
Congratulations, Chief! Here you go, Dad.

140
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:56,800
H-hey, hey.

141
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:59,420
Chief, don't you have anything to say?

142
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,860
Everyone, thank you.

143
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,580
Congratulations.

144
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:11,916
Well then, you lot,

145
00:09:11,966 --> 00:09:14,820
coming all this way just
to celebrate my birthday,

146
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:18,680
Chief, are you crying?

147
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,900
N-no, you idiot, I'm not crying!

148
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:24,040
Here you go, Dad. This is from Mom and me.

149
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,740
Leather shoes?

150
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:33,820
I'll make good use of them.

151
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:39,560
Chief, this is just a little gift from us.

152
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,140
It's rather big, though.

153
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:45,300
I wonder what Senpai ended up buying.

154
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,000
What is this?

155
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:54,960
How about it, Chief? Nostalgic, right?

156
00:09:56,780 --> 00:10:00,480
The department store happened to
be holding a nostalgic dagashi fair.

157
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:04,940
Look, silver balls, menko cards,
silver ball guns, and slingshots.

158
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:09,000
There's also kelp snacks,
sauce crackers, and even pickled squid.

159
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:13,240
And these firecrackers. Back in the day, they
were called nibidan, and they were much bigger.

160
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:17,120
Senpai, don't tell me you spent
all the money we collected on that?

161
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:21,860
Of course. Well, with 20,000 yen,
you can buy quite a lot, can't you?

162
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,980
You didn't know?

163
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:27,960
Since you didn't say you
wanted to pick it yourself,

164
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:31,560
Letting Ryo-chan choose
was a mistake after all.

165
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:34,100
Hey, hey, what is this?

166
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:36,340
What, you don't even know menko?

167
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,080
Okay, just watch.

168
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,720
You do it like this.

169
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,960
If it lands face-down, you win it.

170
00:10:45,340 --> 00:10:47,180
Wow, this is fun!

171
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:51,960
With menko,
you put your hips into it like this,

172
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,180
and you throw it like that.

173
00:10:56,380 --> 00:10:58,200
There's no way I'm losing to the Chief!

174
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:03,120
You really got us there, didn't you?

175
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:11,420
Well? Had enough?

176
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:19,720
You're a lifelong friend, you are.

177
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:22,240
Thank you so much for today.

178
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:24,060
Never mind the gifts themselves,

179
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:27,780
I'm really touched that you
all celebrated my birthday.

180
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:29,980
Never mind the gifts themselves,

181
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,540
You were so wrapped up in
playing with them yourselves.

182
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:35,260
So then,

183
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:39,900
As a token of thanks,
I'd like to treat everyone to some tea.

184
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:41,940
Tea?

185
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:53,380
What is this room?

186
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:55,100
There's practically nothing in here,
is there?

187
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,100
This is the tea room.

188
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:58,840
It's a place for drinking tea.

189
00:11:58,840 --> 00:11:59,520
Tea room?

190
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:00,900
For crying out loud.

191
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:02,860
Even though the house is already so cramped,

192
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:04,960
did he really build a whole
room just for drinking tea?

193
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:06,020
Ryo-chan.

194
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:08,160
You have to sit seiza in here.

195
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,520
Is that so?

196
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:11,380
Geez, what is this?

197
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,260
Please, go ahead.

198
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,680
Thanks, thanks,
you shouldn't have gone to so much trouble.

199
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,780
Well then, we won't stand on ceremony.

200
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:32,720
You can't just dig in right away, you know.

201
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,340
Wait until the Chief comes.

202
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,600
Don't be so stingy,
c'mon, just a little taste.

203
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,240
Well then, please wait a moment.

204
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,080
Hey, Ryo-chan, do you get it?

205
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:49,140
When you drink tea, you do it like this,
slowly turning the teacup

206
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:51,140
I know that much!

207
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:53,400
You turn it around three times or so, right?
Round and round and round.

208
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,340
You idiot.

209
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:57,000
If you turn it vertically,
the tea will spill out, you know.

210
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:57,700
Yeah.

211
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:11,540
Why's he making such a big deal out of it?

212
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:11,800
This

213
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:12,580
Shh.

214
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,640
It's already started, you know.

215
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:20,460
Mm.

216
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,120
Mm.

217
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:26,360
Mm.

218
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:28,400
Mm.

219
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:29,120
Mm.

220
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:32,140
Mm.

221
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:33,400
Mm.

222
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,680
Mm.

223
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:35,980
Mm.

224
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:38,920
Honbu-san, is something wrong?

225
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,740
Ugh, my legs are going numb.

226
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,620
Here, have some sweets.

227
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:45,900
Yo, we've been waiting!

228
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,640
The sweets have finally arrived.

229
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,560
Well then, don't mind if I do.

230
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,840
Hey, you there, barbarian.

231
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,900
You don't understand the
spirit of tea at all, do you,

232
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:04,740
You don't have to do anything,
so just sit there and keep quiet.

233
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,075
Barbarians aside,

234
00:14:09,125 --> 00:14:12,080
I'll have you savor it
from my prized tea bowl.

235
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,360
Tea bowl?

236
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:20,300
This is the thing I treasure most right now.

237
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:21,260
Oh my.

238
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:26,056
I found it on a trip to Kyoto,
and I just had to have it,

239
00:14:26,106 --> 00:14:29,380
so I decided I'd use it for the
rest of my life and splurged on it.

240
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:31,197
A black raku tea bowl, I see.

241
00:14:31,247 --> 00:14:34,400
It seems quite a fine piece.
Kōetsu's work, perhaps?

242
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:38,600
The black luster is wonderful.

243
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:42,180
Let me serve everyone tea in this bowl.

244
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,860
Luster

245
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:48,020
It's just an ordinary tea bowl, isn't it?

246
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:49,680
Ryotsu!

247
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,540
Hey, cut that out!

248
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:53,980
Come on, let us see it.

249
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:54,540
Ryotsu!

250
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:12,320
Whew, that was close, Chief.

251
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,580
Nice catch, Honda!

252
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:17,080
You idiot, be careful!

253
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:20,000
This tea bowl cost 400,000 yen!

254
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,700
What, 400,000?

255
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:23,800
No way... a tea bowl that expensive?

256
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,500
You see, there are things in this world

257
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:29,060
of value that you could never understand.

258
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:44,100
That was a lovely tea ceremony.

259
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,520
Such obvious flattery, how irritating.

260
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:54,300
That was a truly excellent tea ceremony.

261
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,440
It was truly delicious.

262
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,720
As long as you savor it properly,
you don't need to know the etiquette.

263
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:04,728
Well then,

264
00:16:04,778 --> 00:16:09,260
I can't very well make tea for
everyone and not for Ryotsu, can I?

265
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:12,980
Chief, I'd rather have something like ochazuke,
just a quick bowl of rice with tea poured over it.

266
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:16,660
You might be right that it suits you better.

267
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:20,640
But I've got a meal being prepared now,
so hold on a little longer.

268
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:23,780
Dad, there's a phone call for you.

269
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:26,820
I see. Then, Ryotsu, wait here.

270
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:29,600
Don't you dare touch that tea bowl.

271
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:30,560
Everyone!

272
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,680
I know, I know.

273
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:40,420
Is it really going to be okay?

274
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,420
Phew.

275
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,780
Honestly, what's so special
about a 400,000-yen tea bowl?

276
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:47,340
If it's that high and mighty,

277
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,740
it should at least have
a price tag stuck on it.

278
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:53,140
But still,
drinking tea from a 400,000-yen bowl...

279
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:54,840
I was really nervous.

280
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:57,100
Tea utensils look simple,

281
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,340
but they're all pricey, you know.

282
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:02,440
Things like this, you know...

283
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:06,000
This'll be perfect for cleaning my ears.

284
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:09,040
Senpai, that's bad. You shouldn't do that.

285
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,100
That's right.

286
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:12,200
Hey, I don't care!

287
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:16,860
Now then,
allow me to prepare tea for you all.

288
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:20,520
True tea ceremony is

289
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:22,840
just stirring it like this,

290
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,380
like a washing machine.

291
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:28,120
Whirl, whirl, is that how it goes?

292
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:29,500
Hey, stop that.

293
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,910
Whirl, whirl, whirl, whirl,

294
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:34,280
Whirl, I said, whirl, whirl.

295
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:37,620
Ryo-chan, I told you to stop!

296
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:41,340
Whirl, whirl, whirl, whirl, whirl, whirl.

297
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:41,960
Senpai!

298
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:48,260
Uh, I got a little carried away there.

299
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:51,580
R-Ryo-chan.

300
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:52,300
Senpai.

301
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,520
W-why?

302
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:00,140
W-what, w-what, what!

303
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,940
Looks like you finally broke it

304
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:07,600
I-I can't believe it broke so easily!

305
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:10,420
Chief, it must be a fake. We were tricked.

306
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:13,360
Sorry to keep you waiting.

307
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:16,000
Ryotsu, what are you doing?

308
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:22,680
But Chief, this is truly a
beautiful tea bowl, isn't it?

309
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,680
Do you even understand its appeal?

310
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:29,080
Of course I do!

311
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:33,520
The feel of it is so wonderful,
I don't want to let go of it.

312
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:38,720
If you're serious, I'll make tea with it right now,
so give it back quickly.

313
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:43,040
No, no, let me admire it like
this a little longer, please.

314
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:47,640
No way, no way! If I leave it in your hands,
nothing good will come of it!

315
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,520
Come on, give it back now!

316
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:51,500
Just a little longer.

317
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:52,180
No.

318
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:53,660
Really, just a little more.

319
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:56,000
Hey, Ryotsu, that's enough!

320
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,520
What was that?

321
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:03,480
Hey, wait, Ryotsu! Wait!

322
00:19:05,260 --> 00:19:06,720
Is the tea ceremony over?

323
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:09,360
We're getting the barbecue
ready right now, but...

324
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:10,640
Well, that's the thing...

325
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:17,160
A barbecue

326
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:19,320
It'll be ready soon.

327
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:21,040
Thanks.

328
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:21,880
Where are you, Ryotsu?

329
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,580
There you are.

330
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,680
Come on, hand back the bowl already.

331
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:29,700
Hey, Ryotsu!

332
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:34,400
Look, Chief, this bowl looks
even more striking out in nature.

333
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:36,580
Never mind that, just give it back.

334
00:19:36,580 --> 00:19:38,140
What's going on here?

335
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:42,460
You're being rude to our guests.

336
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:45,360
Ryo-chan, please, do help yourself.

337
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:46,400
Sorry.

338
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,000
If you give it back now, I'll forgive you.

339
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,560
Come on, hurry up and give it back.

340
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:53,520
Really?
If I give it back now, you'll forgive me?

341
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:55,460
Yes, a man never takes back his word.

342
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,780
What should I do?

343
00:19:57,540 --> 00:19:58,860
Please, just give it back.

344
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:00,420
You know, Raku-chan breaks easily.

345
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:02,340
What would you do if
this happened every day?

346
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:04,060
You can't undo something like that,
you know.

347
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:04,820
Dear.

348
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,300
What's the matter, acting like a child?

349
00:20:08,300 --> 00:20:11,080
Ryo-san won't get to eat any meat, will he?

350
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:19,380
Dad, just lend that tea to Ryo-san for a while.
No way, you blockhead!

351
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:26,080
How awful, calling our daughter a blockhead!
Sorry, all right? That's fine, isn't it?

352
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Honda-san, it's burning over there. Well, let's dig in.
Ryo-chan, why aren't you eating? It's so delicious.

353
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:42,260
That's right, stop dawdling and eat.

354
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,900
Reiko, feed me, won't you?

355
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,700
No way.

356
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:50,780
Hey, Yotsu, here, have a drink for now.

357
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:53,880
Well then, I won't hold back.

358
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:56,380
That's not something you drink beer from.

359
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,100
There.

360
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:58,480
Not at all.

361
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,980
Saying that to your senior!

362
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:02,020
Come on, just take it.

363
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:04,900
There you go.

364
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:09,580
Honey, your meat's burning.

365
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,400
What was that?

366
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,120
What was it?

367
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:16,980
Was that an optical illusion?

368
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:19,380
I thought the bowl just split in two.

369
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:21,600
Chief, are you already drunk?

370
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,980
That's impossible.

371
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:27,440
Alright, show me the bowl.

372
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:28,380
That's...

373
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:28,920
This is...

374
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:37,540
Nice catch! That bowl...

375
00:21:38,120 --> 00:21:40,180
What on earth did you do?

376
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:46,620
I can't stand having my precious bowl
played with by the likes of you any longer!

377
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:48,100
Hey! Hurry up and give it back!

378
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,180
Wait! Nice catch!

379
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:52,900
Wait, damn it!

380
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:56,440
I can't wait!

381
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:12,780
No, it broke because of the Chief!

382
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:17,554
My, my...

383
00:22:17,604 --> 00:22:21,140
It was my one and only treasure.

384
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:25,160
What am I supposed to
live for from tomorrow on?

385
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:29,340
Come on, Dad. Don't be so down.

386
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:32,680
You can just buy a new one, right?

387
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:34,780
This is delicious.

388
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:35,660
Ryo-chan!

389
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:39,460
Well, if you don't eat quickly,
I'll eat it all myself!

390
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:43,400
Ryo-chan, apologize properly.
The Chief feels terrible, you know.

391
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:49,390
Chief, all things with
form will break someday.

392
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,640
That's the truth of all things.

393
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:54,740
Anyway, let's eat the meat. It's delicious.

394
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:57,780
I don't want any. You eat it.

395
00:22:58,100 --> 00:22:59,500
Well then, don't mind if I do.

396
00:23:01,820 --> 00:23:04,600
Ryo-chan, really. Chief, the truth is...

397
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:06,140
Stop it!

398
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,140
That's how it happened.

399
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:07,760
What?

400
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:11,660
No, Chief, it was just a moment of excitement.
I didn't mean any harm at all.

401
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:15,200
Ryotsu, I won't forgive you!

402
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:20,300
B-Chief.

403
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,170
Chief,

404
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:25,900
I'm not even enjoying the barbecue,
it doesn't taste good.

405
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:27,280
Please stop.

406
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:30,080
Oh no, it's broken!

407
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:32,020
You brought this on yourself, Ryo-chan.

408
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:35,100
What a birthday this
has turned into, Hiromi.

409
00:23:35,460 --> 00:23:38,140
But he seems to be having
quite a good time, Dad.

410
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:40,180
Ryotsu-style charcoal-grilled meat.

411
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:42,520
Hot, hot, sorry.

412
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:45,520
For me,
this is the best present there could be.

413
00:23:45,660 --> 00:23:46,800
Please, I'll never be forgiven!

414
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:50,940
Nakagawa, Reiko, Honda, Hiromi, help me!

415
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:07,780
Height 167 cm, weight 71 kg

416
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:09,740
Vision 2.0 in both eyes

417
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:13,080
Chief, are you really going
to challenge this perfect body?

418
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:15,720
Very well, if you insist on a contest,

419
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:17,620
come at me from any direction.

420
00:24:17,620 --> 00:24:21,060
Next time, it's the Great Cockroach Race,
so see you then.

421
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:37,760
Even if you stop the clock,
time keeps moving on,

422
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:48,000
so don't sulk, laugh it off and keep living.

423
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:57,940
Even if today is rainy,

424
00:24:57,940 --> 00:25:03,540
tomorrow will be sunny.

425
00:25:03,540 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye,

426
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,880
to the unpleasant things, farewell.

427
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:21,500
Oh yeah, let's try living as we please.

428
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,940
Good things will come.

429
00:25:23,940 --> 00:25:30,280
The sun is calling you
from outside the door.

430
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:44,000
Thanks for watching.

